WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.434
-Our next guest is
a talented actress you know

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.334
from shows such as
"Big Little Lies"

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.501
and "The Society."

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.868
She stars as Cassie Lang
in the highly-anticipated

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.734
"Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania,"

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.901
which will be in theaters
and IMAX this Friday.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.267
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.133
-You know I promised your mom
that you would only use

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.934
this stuff
when one of us was around.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.200
It's really dangerous tech.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.667
-I know it's dangerous.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.000
-What if the cops took it
from you, huh?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
What if you lost it?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.567
-I didn't lose the suit.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.367
-You have a suit?
Wait, you have a suit?

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.067
-I know how to take care
of myself, okay.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.200
Trust me.
I'm pretty good at it by now.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.200
-Ouch.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.767
-Look, I didn't mean it
like that.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.801
-I know.
-And I'm sorry.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.133
-It's okay. It's all right.
I get it.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.834
I just think you should get
to have a normal life.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.767
-Dad, a guy dressed like a bee
tried to kill me in my room

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.567
when I was 6.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.400
I've never had a normal life.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.334
-Please welcome back to
the show, Kathryn Newton,

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.501
everybody.

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:01:00.567
♪♪

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:06.567
♪♪

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:08.901
-Welcome!
-Hi. Thank you.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.634
-You look wonderful.
-Thank you.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.167
Hi, everyone.
-This is a very exciting week

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.767
for you last week.
-Yes.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.467
-The film premiere party,
the launch.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.601
-Yeah.
-Then you also had a birthday.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.200
Happy birthday. Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.501
Thank you.
-Happy birthday.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.968
-I know, I feel
like I have never celebrated

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.267
my birthday so much.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:27.734
-Oh, because everywhere
you went --

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.067
-It was my birthday.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.734
The premiere was more
my birthday than my birthday,

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.567
you know.
I got the job, you know,

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.868
what, a year and a half ago now?

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.567
And that was like my birthday.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.400
And then, you know,
they celebrated my birthday

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.634
on the press tour.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.434
Everyone surprised me
on my birthday.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.567
I had to go to Toronto
for a premiere,

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:46.067
and the whole audience sang me
happy birthday.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.067
So if you want to, too,
like, I won't --

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:51.834
-I feel like it's a week ago
and I feel like we shouldn't.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:54.901
-No, no. If you --
No, it's okay.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.234
It's okay.
Thank you so much.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.734
I know you wanted to,
but it's fine.

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.167
-Do you like attention
on your birthday?

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:01.701
Because you're certainly
giving out that vibe.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.200
-No, no.
-No?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.467
-No, I don't.

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.400
Your birthday is, like,
the one day you feel like

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.200
everyone has to tell you
happy birthday.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.067
So you -- I feel like you don't
really like me,

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.267
you just are acting like
you like me.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.400
-You wouldn't want them
to say it on other days.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.334
-[ Laughs ] I don't know.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.868
I mean, that never happened
to me before.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:17.901
-That's true.
-Yeah, I've never --

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.267
-We should start doing that
more.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.901
-Just happy birthday, Seth.
-I feel like it's crazy --

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.734
-Yeah, happy birthday to you.
-Thank you.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.634
-It's lovely to hear --
and I feel like I don't know why

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:25.901
we've kind of, like,
boxed ourselves

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.534
into only saying it on the day.
-Right.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.400
Why would you do that?
-Yeah, why would you do that.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.067
-When you could it say it
every day.

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.667
-Also it's fun because
now we share a birthday.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.300
-Right. We could do it together.
-That's so much fun.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.868
-We can have cake any time
we want.

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.334
-Oh my God, this is -- I feel
like you cracked the code here.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:41.667
This is very exciting.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.334
-I guess the real code is
if you can do a Marvel movie,

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.267
like, every movie, then
it's always your birthday.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.467
-Yeah.
That's the important thing.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.067
-Always.
-I mean, obviously,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.467
a Marvel premiere is a little
unlike any other movie premiere.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.067
-Right.
-Was it a trip to be there?

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:54.200
-It was insane.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.467
I mean, I've been a part
of a fandom before.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:57.834
I was on a show called
"Supernatural,"

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.400
and the fans are incredible.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.634
That's a real fan base show.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:02.968
-That changed my life.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:04.968
But then I went
to the Marvel movie premiere,

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.033
and it was, like, huge.

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.667
The fans are --
it's a huge family.

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.400
It's insane.
I saw some little Cassie Langs.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.634
So that was crazy.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.067
-People dressed up
in your costume.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.200
-Yeah.
-That's very exciting.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.868
-It was really exciting.
It felt real.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.234
That's when it felt real.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.567
-Did you feel as though people
treated you differently

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.567
on the set when you were wearing
the costume?

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.167
Let's just take a look
real quick.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.300
Because I feel like -- look,
in the clip, you looked great.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.334
But this is -- I mean, that's,
like, very impressive.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:31.501
-I look a little different,
huh?

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.868
-Yeah.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.200
Did you enjoy wearing the suit?

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.834
-Oh, I love wearing the suit.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.968
Can't you tell that's why I'm in
a Cassie Lang suit?

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.634
I just am not done cosplaying
Cassie Lang.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:42.934
I did my hair in a ponytail.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:46.701
What I'm trying to say
is I'm a fan of Cassie Lang.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.501
No, definitely people
treated you differently.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:51.667
Like, they were a little quieter
around me.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.801
-Oh, yeah.
-A little more scared.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.767
-Uh-huh.
-I would be scared.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.968
And everyone looked at me like
it was really me.

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.901
Like, they think that's
who you are all of a sudden

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:02.400
when you wear the supersuit.
and I promise you,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.667
I fall just the same in
that thing as I do in this.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.267
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.234
I fell a lot.
-You're a faller.

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:09.634
Everybody says that about you.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.567
I'm a tripper. I fall.
I'm just like Cassie.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.501
Like, I was trying to figure out
how to be in a Marvel movie

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.033
and, like, impress everybody,

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:19.100
and she's a little young hero
trying to impress her dad.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.467
We're very similar.
-There you go.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.167
-Yeah, total messes.
-I would imagine Paul Rudd

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.601
is the perfect person
to spend time with.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.234
Especially on your birthday.
I feel like every time

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.267
I'm with Paul,
I do feel like it's my birthday.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.634
-I know.
That's what I'm saying.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:31.968
You get it.
-Everyday is your birthday.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.467
-Everyday was my birthday
on this movie

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:34.567
because of Paul Rudd.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.801
-Yeah.
-Yeah, he's the best.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.968
He gave me a little gift.

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.567
It's actually from the movie.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:42.934
-It's a prop from the film?

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.868
-It's a prop from the film
that I can't tell you about.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.200
-Yeah.
-So...

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.367
Is it spoiler based?
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.801
-Or are you worried that Paul
will be arrested

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:52.801
for stealing a prop?

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:56.234
-I think both,
now that you mention it.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.534
-Yeah, I think both.
Now that we're talking about it,

00:04:57.534 --> 00:04:58.934
I feel like you should not put
that man in danger.

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:00.868
If you're the reason Rudd goes
to jail,

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.267
no one here will forgive you.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:03.434
-Marvel jail.

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.534
-Marvel jail, yeah.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:05.701
-No, he did.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:06.834
He made it special,
and I'll keep it forever.

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:08.901
-Okay. Well, that's very lovely.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.367
-I've talked in the past about
that you consider yourself

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:13.300
growing up,
you felt a little nerdy.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.534
And then this is both superhero,
which I feel like superheroes

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:19.601
no longer have the sort of
nerd stigma they used to have

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:20.901
because they're very mainstream.
-Right.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.868
-But also there's a great
element of science to this.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.901
So did that scratch the nerd
itch, for lack of a better term?

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.901
-Yeah. Cassie Lang is a genius,
you know?

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.367
She's figuring out
the quantum realm and stuff.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.968
So, after I finished the movie,
I didn't have a job.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.067
I was very bored.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.868
So I signed up for
a physics class at UCLA.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.200
[ Laughs ] And I did that.
And I got an "A," thank you.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.300
-Wow.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.767
So we're the same once again.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.067
-Oh, my God, you're her
and she's you.

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:49.367
You're the same.
-I know.

00:05:49.367 --> 00:05:51.200
I'm just really method,
just like Jonathan Majors.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.000
-Did the UCLA students
notice you when you started

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.400
taking their physics class?
-No.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.801
I was hoping someone would.
-Is that safe to say

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:00.400
that you did not dress
like this?

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.734
-No.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.634
I loved putting my outfits
on, though, for the class.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:06.934
You know, like, I put on
my little blue light glasses

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:08.033
and, like, a sweater vest.

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.467
'Cause I didn't go to college,

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:12.901
so I really was really trying in
my Zoom class to make it real.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:14.601
And it doesn't have
the same effect.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:16.067
-Yeah.
-No.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:18.067
-Do you think you dress like --
when you saw the other kids,

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.701
did you think, "I'm dressing
like kids in college now"

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:23.100
or, "I'm dressing like kids
from '90s movies."

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.100
-Definitely '90s movies that
I thought people dressed like

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.100
now and they don't.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.767
Everyone was in sweatpants.
-Gotcha.

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:30.334
-I was the only one
in a collared shirt.

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:32.100
-Uh-huh. And they were like --
-Yeah. It's okay.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.367
-"Oh, my God, that's so sad.
That's an actress."

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:37.400
-[ Laughs ]
I was acting like a student.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.701
Yeah.

00:06:38.701 --> 00:06:40.834
-Can I check in on your dogs,
please?

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:42.767
-Oh, yes. Thank you. That's
so kind of you to remember.

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:43.767
-Well, we've talked about
your dogs.

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:48.300
You have three poodles,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.434
all of whom are so good at
posing for photographs.

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:52.567
-Yes. That is Jack King,
Ruler of All Floof,

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:53.634
Starlight Rosebud,

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:55.000
Hella-good-boy
Gonna-need-a-big-bank.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.767
And "Ten-Four Ladybird
keep the madness rolling."

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.634
-Okay, now,
what do you call them

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:01.534
if you have to, like,
talk to them quickly?

00:07:01.534 --> 00:07:03.334
-Well, last time,
she really didn't have a name

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.200
because she doesn't really
remember it.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.534
So we call her Ladybird
or Little.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.968
This is Buddy and that's Jack.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:12.701
-Yeah.
-And so, what are the ages

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:13.901
of your dogs here?

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:17.100
-He's about 5, 3, and 2.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.234
And one of them
has a very special skill.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:20.300
Who is the yodeler?

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.868
-The little one
is in love with him,

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:24.767
and so when he barks a lot,
she likes to sing to him.

00:07:24.767 --> 00:07:26.167
She croons.

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:27.267
She's in love, you know.

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.067
She just wants him
to notice her.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:30.467
It's very romantic.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:32.567
-And do you feel like he's
barking, do you think she's --

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:34.901
do you think her crooning
is to calm him down

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:36.634
or just to, like,
be in duet with him?

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.868
In your head,
what are you picturing?

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:40.467
-[ Howls ]

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:41.634
[ Laughs ]

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:43.067
What does that say, you know?

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.734
Like, "I love you. Notice me."
I don't know.

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:47.000
-We actually have videos.
-Oh.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.267
-Should we let the whole
audience decide what this --

00:07:49.267 --> 00:07:53.133
this true just sort of
expression of love.

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:54.534
-The expression,
Valentine's Day.

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:57.033
Happy Valentine's Day.
-Okay, let's see it.

00:07:57.033 --> 00:08:00.100
[ Dogs barking ]

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:09.701
-It really is love.

00:08:09.701 --> 00:08:10.901
-Doesn't it feel like love?

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:12.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.167
-I feel like she's saying,
"What you're looking for

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:16.434
isn't out there.

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:19.934
It's right here on the bed,
man."

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:23.334
-"I'm here. Right here.
Why don't you see me?"

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:27.100
-Last thing, I know
this is a question I'm asking

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.667
knowing full well
you'll avoid it, but phase 5

00:08:29.667 --> 00:08:31.667
of Marvel is very exciting
-Very exciting.

00:08:31.667 --> 00:08:34.200
-Young Avengers.
People talk about the idea

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.901
of Young Avengers.
-What are you talking about?

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:38.734
-I'm just saying if
there was going to be something

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.234
like that,
would you be interested?

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:41.934
-I don't know. Would I?
I mean, like, what?

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:45.834
The thing that's cool was making
this movie was the best project

00:08:45.834 --> 00:08:47.667
of my life, and even if
I'm lucky enough to do

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:49.567
another Marvel movie,
nothing will ever top

00:08:49.567 --> 00:08:51.067
working with Paul Rudd
everyday.

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:53.300
-There you go.
-Ever. So, I don't know.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.267
-Alright, well,
we're certainly happy

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:57.167
you made time for us,
on your birthday no less.

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:58.667
